motions will only be made to Queen (assume that underpromotion is not a legal move)\n- You do not need to track the full-move or half-move count\n\nThe input will be provided, as a string like \"<REDACTED_B64> w kq - 0 1\".\nWhen run on this string, your answer must produce the following output:\n\"<REDACTED_B64> b kq - 0 0\\<REDACTED_B64> b kq - 0 0\\<REDACTED_B64> b kq - 0 0\"\nNote that the final output of the move and halfmove are allowed to be incorrect. So the above is scored properly even though the move numbers are wrong.\n\nWith these exceptions (and only these exceptions) you must implement a fully correct move generator, including:\n- Castling, with proper tracking of castling rights\n- Promotion, except only allow promotion to queen\n- En-passant\n\nThe length of re.json must be under 100,000 [regex, replacement]-pairs long, and under 10 megabytes in total.\n\nYou can look at the provided check.py to verify if your solution is correct. You will be tested on other positions as well.\n"], "completed": false, "concurrent_cells_at_end": 4, "concurrent_cells_at_start": 5, "dotnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 0, "embedded_version": "2.0.50", "ended_et": "2026-11-12T15:51:41.871676-05:00", "ended_on_rejection": false, "endpoint_location": "global", "endpoint_location_mixed": false, "env_cause": null, "env_failure": false, "error": "timeout after 2400s", "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "failure_subclass": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": false, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "stdout", "final_workspace_bytes": 353582, "final_workspace_skip_reason": null, "final_workspace_status": "saved", "final_workspace_tar": "/h2/drift-5140-1103/opus/5140/transcripts/with/opencode_regex-chess_claude-opus-5-5_trial1.workspace.tar.gz", "final_workspace_tar_bytes": 23776, "final_workspace_tar_sha256": "8075398c746cc4ebd9de0c823d2bfe946733508a1933a14802669f9c07496428", "first_after_build": false, "f